        "node_id": "RE_kwDOExPvac4EoA0Y",
        "tag_name": "v1.1.0",
        "target_commitish": "main",
        "name": "v1.1.0 - Toggle ring visibility through JS",
        "draft": false,
        "prerelease": false,
        "created_at": "2022-09-19T22:19:38Z",
        "published_at": "2022-09-19T22:28:51Z",
        "assets": [],
        "body": "This version expands `FocusRingAnimationManager` to also provide a global toggle for whether focus rings will be rendered at all. This is useful for when applications only want to render rings when the user is in a \"keyboard mode\" or for any other reason.\r\n\r\nThe scope of changes is:\r\n\r\n- `FocusRingAnimationManager` -> `FocusRingManager`.\r\n- `FocusRingManager.ringsEnabled` is a boolean indicating whether rings are currently allowed to render.\r\n- `FocusRingManager.setRingsEnabled(enabled: boolean)` is a function to change the `ringsEnabled` value. It will also force the rings to immediately re-render to pick up this value.",
        "reactions": {
